A||||3||recluse||If you break it they will come||||1||
Z||000000||recluse||10-22-2001||11:19 PM||||Passed an 84 coupe on the side of the road in my GT and turned around and stopped.  The guy said it threw a belt. As he was working on it another Fiero pulled up behind me! Another coupe.  He asked if we needed any help and left a few mins later.  As the guy got the belt on and tight it just squeeled and slipped. The slipping was making the belt smoke.  I didn't think of it at the time but I think the alt. might have been locked up and the belt was slipping around it. But they drove off to try to make it home anyways.  I just thought it was cool to have 3 Fieros in the same place and the fact that Fiero owners want to help other Fiero owners.  ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Cheever3000||10-22-2001||11:31 PM||||That's awesome!  I don't think 3 Fieros have ever driven the same road here.<P>Sure hoping he didn't have far to go.  <P>I once stopped to check on a Fiero at the side of the road.  Poor guy was just sleepy and decided to pull over (smart).  He was too out of it to even notice my car.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||recluse||10-22-2001||11:40 PM||||He said he had to go about 7 miles... It didn't sound like it was going to make it, but he had a friend following him.<P>I pass a coupe almost every day on my way home from work and always wave but I never get a wave back... The guy never even looks over.<P>3 Fieros on the same road is VERY rare around here too.  ||||reg||1
